cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this repository, please cite it as below."
title: "Physics-Constrained Quantum Circuit Repair: a leakage-free evaluation protocol, benchmarks and a repair agent"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Pandey"
    given-names: "Alok"
    alias: "alok-108"
    affiliation: "Indian Institute of Technology Patna, India"
repository-code: "https://github.com/alok-108/physics-constrained-quantum-repair"
url: "https://alok-108.github.io/physics-constrained-quantum-repair/"
license: MIT
date-released: "2026-10-24"
abstract: >-
  A leakage-free evaluation protocol, a corrected 1000-circuit benchmark, a 600-program benchmark of dynamic
  circuits, and an oracle-guided repair agent for faulty OpenQASM 3 circuits under superconducting-device
  constraints. Includes LLM-only and LLM-as-tool-controller arms, a real-bug pilot from Bugs4Q, and the
  honest limits of each result. The first release of this repository reported invalid numbers (reference
  leakage); they are kept under legacy_v1/ for audit only.
keywords:
  - quantum software engineering
  - automated program repair
  - OpenQASM 3
  - benchmark
  - Qiskit
